2026-07-30 20:52:50,102 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "How was CRP used for stratification in this protocol", "system_prompt_version": "a0b9615a", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "score": 0.42101613, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "score": 0.00026947918, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "score": 0.0001168284, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "score": 5.967352e-05, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 90, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "score": 5.5622066e-05, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "REPRESENTATIVES OF CRO", "score": 4.947159e-05, "scores": null}], "context_char_count": 5471, "response": "## CRP Use in Stratification \u2014 Protocol CTJ301UC201\n\n### Original Version (v1.0)\n\nIn the **original version** of the protocol, CRP was explicitly used as a stratification factor. Specifically, randomisation was stratified by **elevated (\u22653 mg/L) CRP levels**, along with stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 92).\n\n### Revised Version (v1.1)\n\nIn **Version 1.1**, the stratification factors were **modified** as part of the protocol amendments. CRP was **removed** as a stratification factor, and the randomisation stratification was updated to be based on:\n- **Prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no)**\n- **Consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no)**\n\nThis change is reflected in Sections 3.1.2, 4.2.2, and 9.6.2 of the revised protocol (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 92; p. 36). The Summary of Changes for Version 1.1 explicitly lists \"Modify the randomisation-stratification factors\" and \"Clarify stratification factors in randomization\" as key amendments (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 90).\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Version | Stratification Factors |\n|---|---|\n| v1.0 | Elevated CRP (\u22653 mg/L); stable conventional treatment |\n| v1.1 | Prior corticosteroids (yes/no); consent to PK substudy (yes/no) |\n\n> **Note:** While CRP continued to be measured as a **biomarker** (ESR, CRP, neutrophil and platelet count analysed at local sites) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 45), it was no longer used as a randomisation stratification factor in Version 1.1.", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "1 = 90 patients will be centrally, dynamically, stratified randomly (by elevated ( \u22653 mg/L) CRP levels, and stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs)) assigned to 3 groups (1:1:1) to receive 600mg TJ301 biweekly (Q2W), 300mg TJ301 Q2W or placebo Q2W.. 3.1.2, also in Synopsis, 4.2.2 and 9.6.2, 2 = 90 patients will be centrally, dynamically, randomly assigned to 3 groups (1:1:1) to receive 600mg TJ301 biweekly (Q2W), 300mg TJ301 Q2W or placebo Q2W. Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no).", "bboxes": [[52.59044647216797, 495.76949310302734, 771.7723999023438, 121.96722412109375]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 90, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "Clarify stratification factors in randomization... Modify the randomisation-stratification factors.", "bboxes": [[59.4, 449.0640073242187, 517.92, 438.774999631911]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "exactText": "Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no).", "bboxes": [[72.0, 233.90398291015606, 538.44, 178.01497521784836]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "exactText": "Biomarkers erythrocyte sedimentation rate [ESR], C-reactive protein (CRP), neutrophil and platelet count tests will be analysed in local sites.", "bboxes": [[77.15952000000003, 132.16128732421873, 795.356639999999, 115.30609217037261]], "relevance": "medium"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": false, "embedding_ms": 2369.901416997891, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_search_ms": 1747.5460830028169, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 44, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 44, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.4243, 0.5249, 0.5027, 0.4879, 0.4726, 0.4676, 0.4377, 0.4354, 0.4313, 0.4304, 0.4287, 0.4192, 0.4177, 0.4165, 0.4148, 0.4141, 0.4136, 0.4113, 0.4091, 0.4069, 0.4064, 0.4058, 0.404, 0.403, 0.4023, 0.4008, 0.4003, 0.3998, 0.3979, 0.3977, 0.3976, 0.3959, 0.3959, 0.3948, 0.3946, 0.3941, 0.3941, 0.3916, 0.3901, 0.3872, 0.3868, 0.3862, 0.3861, 0.3858], "confidence_filter_dropped_scores": [], "confidence_filter_bm25_only_scores_normalized": [], "hybrid_search": true, "cache_hit": true, "embedding_ms": 0.0, "db_search_ms": 757.8294589766301, "hybrid_parallel_ms": 1152.0759160048328, "vector_count": 45, "bm25_count": 0, "fused_count": 44, "reranker_enabled": true, "reranker_provider": "cohere", "reranker_ms": 541.2812909926288, "reranker_input_count": 44, "reranker_output_