2026-07-30 20:53:47,098 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "Does this protocol use a DSMC or an SRC to oversee safety data?", "system_prompt_version": "a0b9615a", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 93, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "score": 0.9914225, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 29, "section": "3.3 Safety Review Committee", "score": 0.7490872, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 19, "section": "List of Abbreviations", "score": 0.0006641048, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 13, "section": "Data Analyses", "score": 0.00023413582, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 68, "section": "9.8.1 General Considerations", "score": 0.00013765463, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 16, "section": "Protocol No.: CTJ301UC201", "score": 0.000113234375, "scores": null}], "context_char_count": 4635, "response": "This protocol uses a **Safety Review Committee (SRC)** \u2014 not a DSMC \u2014 to oversee safety data.\n\nThe SRC is described as \"an expert advisory group commissioned and charged with the responsibility of evaluating, primarily, cumulative safety data at regular intervals\" (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 29). The SRC reviews blinded data and provides recommendations to the Sponsor regarding trial conduct and possible trial modifications (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 29).\n\nNotably, the protocol's Version 1.1 change summary explicitly explains the rationale for this terminology: **\"It is more appropriate to use SRC rather than DSMC as the name of the committee, since the purpose of the committee is to review safety data.\"** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 93). This change was applied across multiple sections including the Synopsis, Sections 3.3, 6.1, and 6.2.5 (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 93).\n\nThe SRC must comprise **at least a medical monitor, a physician, and a pharmacologist**, all with relevant experience, and a SRC Working Procedure (charter) must be prepared and signed prior to enrolment of the first patient (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 29).", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 29, "section": "3.3 Safety Review Committee", "exactText": "A Safety Review committee (SRC) will be established. The SRC is an expert advisory group commissioned and charged with the responsibility of evaluating, primarily, cumulative safety data at regular intervals. The SRC will review blinded data and provide recommendations to the Sponsor based on their evaluation.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 579.2639829101564, 555.24, 523.3749752178487]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 93, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "3.3, 3 = It is more appropriate to use SRC rather than DSMC as the name of the committee, since the purpose of the committee is to review safety data.", "bboxes": [[52.683868408203125, 495.55684661865234, 771.1757202148438, 129.38385009765625]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 19, "section": "List of Abbreviations", "exactText": "SRC Safety Review Committee", "bboxes": [[144.00287999999978, 517.0900629101561, 198.72815999999978, 507.62417583323304]], "relevance": "medium"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": false, "embedding_ms": 1639.9849580484442, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_search_ms": 225.70408397587016, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 45, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 45, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kep