2026-07-30 20:55:10,160 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What happens if a patient becomes pregnant during the trial, and what follow-up is required?", "system_prompt_version": "a0b9615a", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 61, "section": "8.4 Pregnancy and Pregnancy Outcome", "score": 0.9428234, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 65, "section": "8.6.1 Follow-up of Adverse Events with Onset during the Trial", "score": 0.8171371, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 51, "section": "6.3 Safety Follow-up Visit (Visit 9)", "score": 0.80162543, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 55, "section": "7.1.4 Clinical Safety Laboratory Parameters", "score": 0.566798, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 33, "section": "3.4.7 Follow-up Procedures", "score": 0.44501695, "scores": null}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 27, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "score": 0.08509905, "scores": null}], "context_char_count": 4739, "response": "## Pregnancy During the Trial\n\n### Immediate Actions\nIf a pregnancy occurs at any time after signing the informed consent form, **the IMP must be immediately stopped** and **the Sponsor must be informed immediately** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n\n### Reporting\n- Pregnancy itself is **not** classified as a Serious Adverse Event (SAE) and should **not** be reported via the e-CRF (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n- Contact details for follow-up on the pregnancy must be provided with the report (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n- The Sponsor may request additional pregnancy-specific follow-up information once the pregnancy has been notified (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n\n### Required Follow-up\n- The **mother and foetus must be followed up at least until the birth of the infant and one month after the birth** of the infant. This also applies to pregnancy following **paternal IMP exposure** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n- Follow-up will generally include:\n  - Course, duration, and outcome of the pregnancy\n  - Neonatal health (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61)\n\n### Abnormal Outcomes\n- If the pregnancy results in an **abnormal outcome** (e.g., birth defect or congenital anomaly), this **must be reported as an SAE** to the Sponsor per the procedure in Section 8.5.2 (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n- Any outcome considered by the Investigator and/or Sponsor to be **related to the IMP** will be treated as an **expedited report** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 61).\n\n### Routine Pregnancy Testing in the Trial\n- A **serum \u00df-HCG and serum pregnancy test** are conducted at the Screening Visit (Visit 1), and **urine pregnancy tests** are conducted at Visit 8 and the Safety Follow-up Visit (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 55; p. 51).", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 61, "section": "8.4 Pregnancy and Pregnancy Outcome", "exactText": "If a pregnancy occurs at any time after signing the informed consent form, the IMP should be immediately stopped and the Sponsor must be informed immediately. Note that pregnancy itself is not an SAE, and should not be reported via the e-CRF. Contact details for the follow up on the pregnancy should be provided with the report. The Sponsor may request additional pregnancy-specific follow-up information once the pregnancy has been notified. The mother and the foetus must be followed-up at least until the birth of the infant and one month after the birth of the infant (also pregnancy following paternal IMP exposure). In general, the follow-up will include the course; duration and the outcome of the pregnancy as well as neonatal health. If a pregnancy results in an abnormal outcome (birth defect/congenital anomaly), this must be reported as an SAE to the Sponsor according to the procedure described in Section 8.5.2. Any outcome which the Investigator and/or the Sponsor considers to be related to the IMP will be treated as an expedited report.", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 173.54398291015616, 523.2, 148.13497521784848]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 55, "section": "7.1.4 Clinical Safety Laboratory Parameters", "exactText": "For female subjects, a serum \u00df-HCG and a serum pregnancy test will be conducted at the Screening Visit (Visit 1) and urine pregnancy tests will be conducted at visit 8 and Follow-up visit.", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999972, 299.06398291015614, 554.1599999999999, 212.81497521784843]], "relevance": "medium"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 51, "section": "6.3 Safety Follow-up Visit (Visit 9)", "exactText": "At the Safety Follow-up Visit, the following data will be collected: ... Urine pregnancy test", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999989, 179.18398291015637, 558.84, 138.5349752178488]], "relevance": "medium"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 65, "section": "8.6.1 Follow-up of Adverse Events with Onset during the Trial", "exactText": "During the trial, the Investigator must follow-up on each adverse event until it is resolved or until the medical condition of the patient is stable.", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 695.9039829101564, 542.64, 670.4949752178487]], "relevance": "low"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": false, "embedding_ms": 228.6089169792831, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_search_ms": 222.37208305159584, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 45, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 45, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0